# binary-path-fence-allow — files exempt from binary-path-fence.sh, one repo-relative path
# per line, `#` comments. Add here only what genuinely IS the build/release/test machinery
# a hardcoded path is unavoidable in; a caller of a binary belongs on spira_bin instead.

# THE BUILD AND RELEASE TOOLING ITSELF — these assemble bin/ or a tarball; they are the
# thing spira_bin's production branch trusts, not a second reader of it.
Makefile
spira/build-tarball.sh
spira/pre-activate.sh
spira/acceptance-lib.sh

# conf.sh's spira_config_bin(): a pre-cutover, memoized ad-hoc build kept for the one
# caller (lib.sh persona_model) that may run before conf.sh's own SPIRA_CONFIG_BIN
# resolution has happened. Out of scope for sp-zv7j4's testenv-batch rewrite.
spira/conf.sh

# testlib_spira_config_bin() — a suite fixture needs SPIRA_CONFIG_BIN resolved BEFORE it
# can source conf.sh at all (conf.sh needs the binary to convert spira.conf), so it cannot
# itself go through spira_bin.
spira/testlib.sh

# spira-loom.service deliberately runs from the dev checkout, never a release (its own
# comment explains why) — its ExecStart path is that deliberate exception, not a bug.
systemd/spira-loom.service

# systemd unit templates render via @KEY@ substitution (render.py), not a shell that could
# call spira_bin — spira-lc.service is inert (sp-uwv2s) and has no render.py plumbing yet
# for a resolved SPIRA_LC_BIN placeholder; wiring one is follow-up work.
systemd/spira-lc.service

